<title>ITALY: Mannesmann wants bigger Omnitel stake - paper.</title>
<headline>Mannesmann wants bigger Omnitel stake - paper.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German industrial group Mannesmann AG wants to increase its stake in Italy's second mobile phone group Omnitel and could do this by a purchase from Olivetti, reports financial daily Il Sole 24 Ore.</p>
<p>Mannesmann currently holds a stake of around six percent in Omnitel, and the report suggests it is in preliminary talks to acquire a further eight percent stake in Omnitel from Olivetti.</p>
<p>Current shareholders of Omnitel are Olivetti with 41.3 percent, Airtouch Communications with 11.7 percent and Bell Atlantic Corp with 11.6 percent.</p>
<p>Omnitel was holding a news conference today and no-one was available to comment immediately on the newspaper report.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
